> One important compatibility caveat: many provider APIs only permit `role="tool"` if the immediately preceding assistant message contains a provider-native `tool_calls` entry with a matching `tool_call_id`. Your plan footer is not presently such a call.
> 
> So define this as a **planner-normalized transcript**, then have each model adapter render it appropriately:
> 
> - providers supporting standalone tool messages: send it directly;
> - OpenAI-style strict APIs: synthesize a matching assistant `tool_call` and matching tool result;
> - providers without tool roles: serialize it into a clearly delimited, untrusted context block—not a system message.
> 
> The `tool` role improves semantics and provenance, but does not itself make tool content trusted.
